    "name": "message_peer",
    "description": "Send a short plain-text message to another live Claude session on this machine (call list_peers first for names). Use sparingly, only to coordinate on shared files or hand off one fact. The user can see every message; exchanges are hop-limited and the receiver may not answer. Never include secrets."
   },
   {
    "name": "claim_files",
    "description": "Announce that you are working on specific files or folders so other Claude sessions stay out. Other sessions are paused on their first edit to a claimed path and told to message you. Paths are relative to the repo root; a folder claims everything under it and * / ** patterns work. Claims expire (default 60 minutes, max 480) or end when you call release_claims. Use it for real multi-edit work, not for a single small change."
   },
   {
    "name": "release_claims",
    "description": "Release claims you made with claim_files. Pass paths to release just those, or nothing to release all of yours."
